write('about',layout({title:'Why SpenceCom? Meet Amit & Our Team | Professional IT Engineering Philippines',description:'Meet Amit Kumar, Spencer, Dharul and Aldrian. Learn why SpenceCom brings Singapore-backed root-cause IT engineering, managed networks, cloud, automation and AI to Angeles City, Clark and the Philippines.',canonical:'/about/',body:innerHero('OUR STORY / OUR X FACTOR','We fix the cause.<br><em>Not just the symptom.</em>','Founded on a simple belief: every business deserves properly engineered technology—not a temporary fix that fails again tomorrow.')+`
<section class="section about-story"><div class="container about-founder"><div class="about-founder-photo"><img src="/assets/images/team-amit.webp" alt="Amit Kumar working on a Mac laptop at his desk" width="139" height="165"/><div class="portrait-note">Amit Kumar · Technology &amp; Strategy</div></div><article class="rich-content"><span class="eyebrow">WHY SPENCECOM EXISTS</span><h2>From Singapore experience to a smarter standard of IT in the Philippines.</h2><p class="lead">Coming from Singapore, Amit Kumar saw an opportunity to bring more structured, forward-looking technology engineering to businesses in Angeles City, Clark and across the Philippines.</p><p>Many businesses have experienced the familiar cycle: Wi-Fi drops, a technician restarts a router, everything seems fine—until it happens again. Hardware may be replaced without testing the cable, checking the logs, examining congestion or understanding the business workflow. The immediate symptom disappears, but the underlying risk remains.</p><p>That is the problem SpenceCom was created to address. Drawing on <strong>more than two decades across IT, websites, servers and infrastructure</strong> through <a href="https://axon.com.sg/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Axon 1Pro's Singapore roots, established in 2002</a>, Amit wanted to extend that practical expertise into an integrated, hands-on service for the Philippine market.</p><p>We believe a business network is more than cables and computers. It includes employees, documents, cloud applications, backups, security, collaboration and now AI. A solution is not complete simply because a device turns on. It should improve reliability, reduce repetitive work, protect business continuity and make people more productive.</p><blockquote class="about-quote">“If it works today, will it keep working tomorrow? We measure, investigate and solve the root cause—then connect the whole system so the business can move forward.”<span>— Amit Kumar</span></blockquote><p>Whether you are a small team using personal email accounts or a growing organisation with multiple offices, we can assess the existing setup, plan a move to professional email and cloud tools, and introduce automation or private AI where it genuinely helps. We believe these advantages should be accessible to businesses of different sizes—not reserved for large enterprises.</p><p>Our starting point is a <strong>free initial consultation</strong> to understand your environment and explain the choices clearly. No unnecessary hardware replacement. No promise that AI solves everything. Just an honest path from today's problems to tomorrow's working system.</p><p class="about-origin-note">Axon 1Pro's 2002 date refers to the backing Singapore consultancy, not the founding date of SpenceCom.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section about-difference"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">OUR X FACTOR</span><h2>Quick-fix support vs.<br><em>professional IT engineering.</em></h2><p class="about-section-intro">A practical comparison of two approaches—not a judgement about every IT technician. Tools, process, integration and accountability make the difference.</p><div class="approach-grid"><article class="approach-card reactive"><span class="approach-marker">THE REACTIVE APPROACH</span><h3>Make it work.<br>For now.</h3><div class="approach-scene"><span class="scene-device">Wi-Fi drops</span><span class="scene-arrow">↓</span><span class="scene-action">Restart router</span><span class="scene-arrow">↓</span><span class="scene-device">Problem returns</span></div><ul><li><strong>Symptom:</strong> restart or replace the device</li><li><strong>Diagnosis:</strong> guesswork without measurement</li><li><strong>Scope:</strong> only the broken component</li><li><strong>Handover:</strong> little documentation or baseline</li><li><strong>Outcome:</strong> recurring calls and avoidable downtime</li></ul></article><article class="approach-card engineered"><span class="approach-marker">THE SPENCECOM APPROACH</span><h3>Understand it.<br>Engineer it right.</h3><div class="approach-scene professional-scene"><span class="scene-device">Inspect &amp; measure</span><span class="scene-arrow">↓</span><span class="scene-action">Find root cause</span><span class="scene-arrow">↓</span><span class="scene-device">Validate &amp; monitor</span></div><ul><li><strong>Diagnosis:</strong> site surveys, logs, packet captures and cable tests where needed</li><li><strong>Design:</strong> LAN, Wi-Fi, NAS, cloud and users considered together</li><li><strong>Implementation:</strong> staged changes, testing and rollback plans</li><li><strong>Handover:</strong> documented topology, access and recovery steps</li><li><strong>Outcome:</strong> reliable operations and room for automation</li></ul></article></div><div class="about-toolnote"><strong>Professional tools. Measurable results.</strong><p>Network analysers, cable testers, Wi-Fi surveys, monitoring dashboards, server logs and backup-restore checks help turn assumptions into evidence. The exact tools depend on the issue; our process is built around proving the result.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section about-values"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">WHAT WE DO DIFFERENTLY</span><h2>Hardware is only the start.<br><em>Productivity is the goal.</em></h2><div class="about-value-grid"><div><span>01</span><h3>Look at the whole business</h3><p>We review how devices, staff, networks, storage and applications actually work together.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Keep what works</h3><p>We assess existing infrastructure before recommending upgrades or replacements.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Modernise intelligently</h3><p>Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, professional email, cloud migration, smart offices and private AI—when appropriate.</p></div><div><span>04</span><h3>Deliver on-site and remotely</h3><p>Real installation and commissioning in the Philippines, with suitable cloud and AI projects supported worldwide.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section about-team"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">THE PEOPLE BEHIND THE WORK</span><h2>Meet the <em>SpenceCom team.</em></h2><p class="about-section-intro">Technology should feel personal. You'll know the people responsible for the planning, engineering, installation and support.</p><div class="team-grid"><article class="team-card"><div class="team-portrait"><img src="/assets/images/team-amit.webp" alt="Amit Kumar working at his Mac laptop" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="team-card-copy"><span>TECHNOLOGY &amp; STRATEGY</span><h3>Amit Kumar</h3><p>Leads solution strategy across business IT, web, servers, cloud, automation and AI. Brings the Singapore-backed experience and whole-system perspective behind SpenceCom.</p></div></article><article class="team-card"><div class="team-portrait"><img src="/assets/images/team-spencer.webp" alt="Portrait of Spencer, SpenceCom engineer" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="team-card-copy"><span>ENGINEERING</span><h3>Spencer</h3><p>Network and systems engineering, on-site implementation and turning technical plans into working business infrastructure.</p></div></article><article class="team-card"><div class="team-portrait team-coming"><span>PHOTO<br>COMING SOON</span></div><div class="team-card-copy"><span>FIELD TECHNICIAN</span><h3>Dharul</h3><p>Supports field installation, structured cabling, site preparation and hands-on equipment setup.</p></div></article><article class="team-card"><div class="team-portrait team-coming"><span>PHOTO<br>COMING SOON</span></div><div class="team-card-copy"><span>TECHNICAL SUPPORT</span><h3>Aldrian</h3><p>Technical assistance, user support and helping clients confidently adopt their new workplace tools.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section client-section"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">LOCAL PROJECT EXPERIENCE</span><h2>Trusted relationships.<br><em>Real projects.</em></h2><p>Examples of Philippine organisations connected with our consulting and implementation work.</p><div class="client-logos">${clientLogos.map(([name,src,url])=>`<a href="${url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="client-logo" aria-label="${esc(name)}"><img loading="lazy" src="${src}" alt="${esc(name)} logo" /></a>`).join('')}</div><div class="mini-divider"></div><span class="eyebrow">AXON 1PRO SINGAPORE HERITAGE</span><p>Selected names appearing in Axon 1Pro's historical client portfolio; these relationships are attributed to Axon, not represented as contracts directly awarded to SpenceCom.</p><div class="client-logos">${axonClientLogos.map(([name,src])=>`<div class="client-logo"><img loading="lazy" src="${src}" alt="${esc(name)} client logo" /></div>`).join('')}</div><p class="client-caption"><a href="https://axon.com.sg/testimonials.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View the original Axon client and testimonial page ↗</a></p></div></section>`+contactCta}));
const articles=[
 ['office-wifi-upgrade','How to Plan a Business Wi-Fi 6 or Wi-Fi 7 Upgrade','The right access point count depends on site layout, density, interference and roaming needs. Start with a survey, not a router purchase.'],
 ['microsoft-google-email-migration','Microsoft 365 vs Google Workspace Migration: What to Check','Mailbox data is only one part of a migration. Consider identity, calendars, shared files, devices, DNS, security and user training.'],
 ['nas-cloud-private-ai','Connecting NAS, Cloud Storage and Private AI Safely','Secure document search requires explicit source approval, identity controls, permission-aware retrieval and ongoing data lifecycle checks.'],
 ['traditional-vs-modern-business-network','Traditional LAN vs Modern Managed Business Network','Compare unmanaged flat networks against segmented VLANs, PoE, managed 2.5GbE/10GbE, central monitoring and resilient dual-WAN connectivity.'],
 ['traditional-vs-modern-office','Traditional Office vs Smart AI-Enabled Workplace','Compare disconnected meeting rooms, manual administration and isolated files against cloud-enabled collaboration, intelligent AV and practical automation.'],
 ['traditional-vs-modern-wifi','Basic Wi-Fi vs Managed Wi-Fi 6E and Wi-Fi 7','Learn why a single consumer router is different from site-surveyed access points with fast roaming, guest isolation, central policies and capacity planning.'],
 ['traditional-backup-vs-modern-resilience','USB Backup vs Modern NAS, Snapshots and Offsite Recovery','Why a single external drive is not a complete recovery strategy, and how snapshots, immutable copies, offsite replication and test restores improve resilience.'],
 ['linux-vs-windows-call-center','Linux Desktop vs Windows Licensing for Call Centres','Assess when Linux Mint Cinnamon, browser-based CRM, VoIP and cloud desktops can reduce OS licence costs—and when Windows compatibility is essential.'],
 ['traditional-support-vs-ai-operations','Reactive IT Support vs Proactive Monitoring and AI Assistance','Compare break-fix support with monitored infrastructure, documented workflows, permission-aware assistants and human escalation.']
 ,['free-chatbots-vs-private-business-ai','Free ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini vs Private Company AI','When free chatbots are suitable, when managed paid AI helps, and how private or local models can search approved company knowledge safely.']
];
const comparisons={
 'traditional-vs-modern-business-network':['Traditional: unmanaged switches, one flat network, ad hoc cables, a single router and no visibility into bottlenecks.','Modern: managed PoE and multi-gigabit switches, documented Cat6A, VLAN separation for staff/guests/IoT, dual-WAN resilience and centrally monitored performance.','Best first step: audit switch capabilities, cabling, traffic, WAN failover and segmentation needs.'],
 'traditional-vs-modern-office':['Traditional: meeting rooms with tangled HDMI cables, stand-alone displays, manual visitor handling and files scattered across local PCs.','Modern: unified conferencing, wireless presentation, calendar-connected rooms, smart energy and access systems, cloud collaboration and useful workflow automation.','Best first step: map high-friction tasks, meeting-room use and user adoption before purchasing devices.'],
 'traditional-vs-modern-wifi':['Traditional: one router or unplanned repeaters, congested channels, dead zones, weak roaming and a shared password for everyone.','Modern: site-surveyed Wi-Fi 6E/7 access points, correct PoE and switching, capacity planning, managed roaming, separate guest networks and continuous RF monitoring.','Best first step: measure coverage, interference, device density and backhaul before selecting access points.'],
 'traditional-backup-vs-modern-resilience':['Traditional: occasional USB copy, backup drive always connected and no restore testing.','Modern: scheduled NAS snapshots, separate offsite/cloud copies, controlled retention, access restrictions, ransomware recovery design and documented test restores.','Best first step: define recovery time and recovery point objectives for each critical system.'],
 'linux-vs-windows-call-center':['Traditional: every workstation depends on locally installed software and a Windows OS licence, whether or not the application requires it.','Modern: validated Linux Mint desktop or thin-client deployments for browser-based CRM, WebRTC softphones, identity, remote access and cloud productivity.','Best first step: pilot the exact dialler, recording, security, headset, browser and vendor-supported applications.'],
 'traditional-support-vs-ai-operations':['Traditional: technicians respond only after an outage, employees search shared folders manually and support knowledge stays in people’s heads.','Modern: infrastructure monitoring, change documentation, automated alerts, searchable authorised company knowledge and AI triage that escalates to a human.','Best first step: inventory incidents, documentation and identity permissions before automating.']
 ,'free-chatbots-vs-private-business-ai':['General public chatbots are useful for low-risk tasks but do not automatically know company documents or enforce each employee’s internal file permissions.','A managed business AI or appropriately secured private/local LLM can connect to approved NAS, SharePoint and Google Drive sources, cite answers and assist workflows with access controls.','Best first step: identify real employee questions, classify the documents and pilot a small permission-aware knowledge assistant before committing to licences or infrastructure.']
};
write('insights',layout({title:'Technology Insights — Smart Wi-Fi, Cloud, NAS & Private AI',description:'Practical technology guides from SpenceCom on wireless networking, Microsoft and Google migration, NAS and private AI integration.',canonical:'/insights/',body:innerHero('IDEAS & EXPERTISE','Useful knowledge.<br><em>Without the hype.</em>','Practical perspectives on making existing networks, cloud platforms and AI work better together.')+`<section class="section"><div class="container insight-grid">${articles.map(([slug,title,excerpt],i)=>`<a class="insight-card" href="/insights/${slug}/"><span class="eyebrow">INSIGHT 0${i+1}</span><h2>${esc(title)}</h2><p>${esc(excerpt)}</p><span>Read guide ↗</span></a>`).join('')}</div></section>`}));
for(const [slug,title,excerpt] of articles){write(`insights/${slug}`,layout({title,description:excerpt,canonical:`/insights/${slug}/`,body:breadcrumb([{name:'Insights',href:'/insights/'},{name:title}])+innerHero('TECHNOLOGY INSIGHTS',esc(title),excerpt)+`<section class="section"><div class="container prose-narrow"><h2>Start with the real requirements.</h2><p>${esc(excerpt)}</p><p>Every organisation has different infrastructure, constraints and security requirements. Document the current systems, the business outcomes, the people affected and the expected risks before selecting technology.</p><h3>A practical checklist</h3><ul><li>Map the current environment and dependencies</li><li>Agree the business outcome and acceptance criteria</li><li>Consider identity, access and security implications</li><li>Test integrations with representative workflows</li><li>Document the change and plan future maintenance</li></ul><p>SpenceCom can help assess the options and build a practical implementation plan for businesses across the Philippines and remote clients worldwide.</p><a class="button button-teal" href="/contact/">Ask an expert ↗</a></div></section>`+contactCta,schema:[{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Article',headline:title,description:excerpt,author:{'@type':'Organization',name:'SpenceCom'},publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'SpenceCom'},mainEntityOfPage:base+`/insights/${slug}/`}]}));}
write('contact',layout({title:'Free IT, Smart Workplace, Cloud & AI Consultation',description:'Contact SpenceCom for business network, Wi-Fi, NAS, Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, cloud server and private AI projects in the Philippines and remotely worldwide.',canonical:'/contact/',body:innerHero('LET’S CONNECT','Tell us what you<br><em>want to achieve.</em>','Start with a free introductory consultation. Based in Angeles City and Clark, available for projects nationwide and appropriate remote engagements worldwide.')+`<section class="section"><div class="container contact-layout"><div><span class="eyebrow">PROJECT ENQUIRIES</span><h2>Let's explore the possibilities.</h2><p>Tell us about your current technology, business goals and project location. We'll respond with sensible next steps.</p><div class="contact-facts"><div><b>Our base</b><span>Angeles City & Clark, Pampanga, Philippines</span></div><div><b>Service coverage</b><span>Philippines nationwide · Worldwide remote</span></div><div><b>Initial consultation</b><span>Complimentary</span></div></div></div><form class="contact-form" id="enquiry-form"><label>Your name<input name="name" required autocomplete="name" placeholder="Full name" maxlength="120"></label><label>Business email<input name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@company.com" maxlength="200"></label><label>Company / organisation<input name="company" placeholder="Company name" maxlength="160"></label><label>Project location<input name="location" placeholder="e.g. Clark, Manila, Cebu or worldwide remote" maxlength="160"></label><label>What can we help with?<select name="service"><option value="">Choose a service</option>${services.map(x=>`<option>${esc(x[1])}</option>`).join('')}<option>Other / multiple services</option></select></label><label>Tell us about your project<textarea name="message" required rows="5" placeholder="Current setup, goals and timing…" maxlength="4000"></textarea></label><p class="form-note">This form prepares an email to our enquiries address; it does not transmit information to a website backend.</p><button type="submit" class="button button-teal">Prepare enquiry email ↗</button></form></div></section>`}));
const assets=path.join(root,'assets');fs.cpSync(assets,path.join(out,'assets'),{recursive:true});
fs.copyFileSync(path.join(root,'web','styles.css'),path.join(out,'styles.css'));
fs.copyFileSync(path.join(root,'web','app.js'),path.join(out,'app.js'));
const routes=['/','/solutions/','/equipment-solutions/','/service-areas/','/about/','/insights/','/contact/',...services.map(x=>`/solutions/${x[0]}/`),...places.map(x=>`/service-areas/${x[0]}/`),...articles.map(x=>`/insights/${x[0]}/`)];
